# ── Fullstack example build output ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Each use case carries a self-contained Scalus (sbt) and Java (Gradle) project.
# Their compiled output is regenerated by `sbt`/`./gradlew` and must not be
# committed — it is the bulk of the untracked noise in this repo.

# Scalus / sbt: compiled classes, generated sources, and Build Server Protocol
# metadata. sbt nests its own build definitions, so `target` appears at several
# depths (`target`, `project/target`, `project/project/target`) — hence the
# recursive match. `project/build.properties` and `project/plugins.sbt` are real
# sources and stay tracked.
*/fullstack/scalus/**/target/
*/fullstack/scalus/.bsp/

# Java / Gradle. `build/` is already covered by the global rule above; these are
# the two it misses: Gradle's per-project cache and the class output some IDEs
# write to `bin/` instead.
*/fullstack/java/.gradle/
*/fullstack/java/app/bin/
# CI runner workspace scratch (report job)
artifacts/
/report.md
*.history
